  Three functions are included, copied verbatim into omni_extract_bench/normalize.py and
  marked there: `canonical` (as `_upstream_canonical`), `unwrap`, and
  `_drop_datalab_sidecars`. They are copied rather than reimplemented so that scores
  produced here remain identical to the upstream metric on the same inputs --
  reimplementing string normalisation risks silent divergence.

  The full grader was vendored at omni_extract_bench/vendor/longextract_bench/ until these
  three were the only parts still reachable from the scoring path. Nothing else from it is
  used: this repo scores through omni_extract_bench/score.py alone.
  (documented there) rather than by editing the vendored source, so the vendored copy
  stays a faithful copy of the original.
